  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5492",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological activity against NCI-H2347 through multiple pathways, with the target NCI-H2347 being engaged by several compounds. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to NCI-H524, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, and subsequently to NCI-H2347. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to A704, which is a target of Racotumomab, and then to NCI-H2347. The third pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is also a target of palmarumycin CP18, and then to NCI-H2347. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence the activity of NCI-H2347. The evidence supports a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating the biological response of NCI-H2347, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with multiple targets and potential mechanisms contributing to the observed effects.",
